+The HDR color $c_{h,i}$ is view-dependent and modeled using Spherical Harmonics (SH) [S1]. Let $k = \{k_{lm} \mid 0 \le l \le L, -l \le m \le l\} \in \mathbb{R}^{(L+1)^2 \times 3}$ be the SH coefficients, where each $k_{lm} \in \mathbb{R}^3$ corresponds to RGB components [S1]. For a view direction $d = (\theta, \phi)$, the HDR color is:
 $$ c_{h,i}(d, k) = \exp\left( \sum_{l=0}^{L} \sum_{m=-l}^{l} k_{lm} Y_{lm}(\theta, \phi) \right) $$
 where $Y_{lm}: S^2 \to \mathbb{R}$ are the SH basis functions [S1].
